[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G  \u001b[6Gyou lose it, every client has to be given the n\u001b[54Gw\u001b[56Gk\u001b[58Gy.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mDecide how players get the public key.\u001b[22m Either\u001b[52Gship it in\u001b[63Gthe\u001b[67Gclient's\u001b[76Gconfig\u001b[83Gor\u001b[86Gbuild,\u001b[93Gor\u001b[96Gpublish\u001b[104Git\u001b[107Gsomewhere\u001b[117Gthey\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gtrust. If that somewhere is your website, the\u001b[53Gite\u001b[57Gneeds\u001b[63GHTTPS. A free Let's\u001b[83GEncrypt certificate covers that, and\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bit'\u001b[10G separate fr\u001b[24G J01.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BPinned\u001b[10Gkeys\u001b[15Gcome\u001b[20Gwith\u001b[25Gone\u001b[29Gtrade-off:\u001b[40Gchanging\u001b[49Gthe\u001b[53Gserver's\u001b[62Gkey\u001b[66Gmeans\u001b[72Gupdating\u001b[81Gevery\u001b[87Gclient.\u001b[95GAvoiding\u001b[104Gthat\u001b[109Gwould\u001b[115Gneed\u001b[120Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bs\u001b[5Gg\u001b[7Ging key\u001b[15Gthat\u001b[20Gvouches fo\u001b[31G rotating server keys. That i\u001b[61Gn't in the\u001b[72Gplan a\u001b[79Gd\u001b[81Gisn't\u001b[87Gneeded now.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BI\u001b[5Gchecked\u001b[13GManifest's\u001b[24GD-081\u001b[30G(libsodium,\u001b[42Gno\u001b[45GTLS\u001b[49Gover\u001b[54GUDP).\u001b[60GThe\u001b[64Gexact\u001b[70Ghandshake,\u001b[81Gand\u001b[85Gwhether\u001b[93Gthe\u001b[97Gpinned\u001b[104Gkey\u001b[108Gships\u001b[114Gin\u001b[117Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbuild or in config, aren't\u001b[30Gdesigned yet.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBrewed for 21s · done 8:26 am\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mgo ahead and start J01. I have a website with SSL already taken care of. I think we should at least initially ship \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255