[0.012, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[7G\u001b[2m10\u001b[10G\u001b[22mseali\u001b[16Gg is r\u001b[23Gfused, so `Send`\u001b[40Greturns fals\u001b[53G and \u001b[59Ghe welcome or hello path closes as\u001b[94Gbefore.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m… +31 lines \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m she\u001b[13Gl command \r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe thoroughness instruction\u001b[32Gis\u001b[35Gin\u001b[38Gthe\u001b[42Gprompt\u001b[49Gand\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Greply\u001b[63Gto\u001b[66Ground\u001b[72G1\u001b[74Gis\u001b[77Gwritten.\u001b[86GStarting\u001b[95Ground\u001b[101G2.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;107;128m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mBackground command \"Run\u001b[27Gcross-review\u001b[40Ground\u001b[46G2\"\u001b[49Gfailed\u001b[56Gwith\u001b[61Gexit\u001b[66Gcode\u001b[71G1\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  build/reviews/feature-base/round-2.md\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ Propose a solution to the problem of waiting idle on the gate while each piece of work completes. I thought we set up\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mworktrees? Did you only set it up so one at a time could work? Can you expand it to have three worktrees in \u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mparallel? One could be waiting on the gate or adversarial review, another could be having work actively performed on \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mit, and a third one if I find I have spare time in between the first two. I want to make use of the caches that \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mcurrently exist, so reusing the same spare worktrees from one run to another would be good if it's not problematic.\u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;225;138;67m✢\u001b[3GBrewing… \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(18m 34s · ↓\u001b[25G22.7k tokens · \u001b[38;2;182;167;120mstill thinking with high effort\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m)\u001b[73G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0031 ─\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[2mPress up to edit queued messages\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[38C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to interrupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
