[0.077, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;107;128m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mBackground command \"Run\u001b[27Gcross-review\u001b[40Ground\u001b[46G2\"\u001b[49Gfailed\u001b[56Gwith\u001b[61Gexit\u001b[66Gcode\u001b[71G1\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRound 2 brought\u001b[19Gmore\u001b[24Gchanges,\u001b[33Gand\u001b[37Gthe\u001b[41Gserious\u001b[49Gone\u001b[53Gis\u001b[56GF5:\u001b[60Gthe\u001b[64Gclient\u001b[71Gsent\u001b[76Gits\u001b[80Gtoken\u001b[86Gbefore\u001b[93Gconfirming\u001b[104Gthe\u001b[108Gserver's\u001b[117Gkey\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwas\u001b[7Ggenuine,\u001b[16Gso\u001b[19Gan\u001b[22Gimpostor\u001b[31Gcould\u001b[37Gcapture\u001b[45Git.\u001b[49GI'm\u001b[53Gfixing\u001b[60Gthat\u001b[65Gwith\u001b[70Ga\u001b[72Gsigned\u001b[79Gcheck\u001b[85Gthe\u001b[89Gclient\u001b[96Gverifies\u001b[105Gbefore\u001b[112Gsending,\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gthe\u001b[7G turning to\u001b[19GF6 and F4.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPropose a solution to the problem of waiting idle on the gate while each piece of work completes. I thought we set up\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mworktrees? Did you only set it up so one at a time could work? Can you expand it to have three worktrees in \u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mparallel? One could be waiting on the gate or adversarial review, another could be having work actively performed on \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit, and a third one if I find I have spare time in between the first two. I want to make use of the caches that \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcurrently exist, so reusing the same spare worktrees from one run to another would be good if it's not problematic.\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[39m Searching for \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m pattern…\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[5B\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
