[0.447, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mHeavy work takes turns.\u001b[22m The memory not\u001b[45G says nothing runs b\u001b[67Gide clang. RAM is the reason: with your local AI\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1Boaded\u001b[13G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mstrata-host\u001b[39m), two full-w\u001b[39Gdth build\u001b[49G would thrash.\u001b[64GSo \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mscripts/ci.sh\u001b[81G\u001b[39mand a\u001b[87Gsmall \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mscripts/heavy.sh <cmd>\u001b[116G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwrapper share one machine-wide lock\u001b[42G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mflock ~/.cach\u001b[57G/jettison/heavy.lock\u001b[39m). A second\u001b[89Ggate\u001b[94Gor\u001b[97Gbuild\u001b[103Gqueues\u001b[110Gbehind\u001b[117Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gfirst instead of competing with it. Reviews,\u001b[51Gedit\u001b[58G, reading and docs need\u001b[82Gno\u001b[85Glock. That's where the \u001b[109Gverlap\u001b[116Gpays\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Boff: the 10-minute review\u001b[32Grounds and\u001b[43Gthe gate's wait no longer leave me idle.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mA lane state file:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/lane.md\u001b[39m in\u001b[42Geach lane, ignored by git, says what the lane holds\u001b[94Gand what\u001b[103Git's waiting on,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bso I always kn\u001b[21Gw\u001b[23Gwhich lane \u001b[35Gs free.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mManifest\u001b[15G\u001b[22mgets the same three lanes, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/manifest.lane-b\u001b[69G\u001b[39mand \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m-c\u001b[39m, each building\u001b[91Gagainst\u001b[99Gthe\u001b[103Gengine\u001b[110Glane\u001b[115Gof\u001b[118Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gsame name.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mDocs:\u001b[22m a \"Lanes\" section i\u001b[32G \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild-and-gates.md\u001b[39m,\u001b[53Ga\u001b[55Gpointer\u001b[63Gin\u001b[66G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mAGENTS.md\u001b[39m,\u001b[77