[0.244, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPropose a solution to the problem of waiting idle on the gate while each piece of work completes. I thought we set up\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mworktrees? Did you only set it up so one at a time could work? Can you expand it to have three worktrees in \u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mparallel? One could be waiting on the gate or adversarial review, another could be having work actively performed on \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mit, and a third one if I find I have spare time in between the first two. I want to make use of the caches that \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mcurrently exist, so reusing the same spare worktrees from one run to another would be good if it's not problematic.\u001b[39m   \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, listed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m directory, ran \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mHere's the worktree proposal.\u001b[33GI'll keep w\u001b[45Grking on\u001b[54GJ01 while you read it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhy it's one at a time now.\u001b[22m Worktrunk is set\u001b[48Gup, but there's\u001b[64Gonly\u001b[69Gone checkout (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgit worktree list\u001b[39m shows\u001b[107Gjust this\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bone). Two settings also work against reuse:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/.config/worktrunk/config.toml\u001b[39m puts new\u001b[46Gworktrees in\u001b[59G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/worktrees/jettison/<branch>\u001b[39m. ccache\u001b[97Gonly\u001b[102Gsha\u001b[106Ges \u001b[110Gompiled\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bobjects\u001b[13Gbetween trees under \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects\u001b[39m (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCCACHE_BASEDIR\u001b[39m), so a\u001b[67Gworktree made\u001b[81Gthere\u001b[87Gwou\u001b[91Gd\u001b[93Gshare nothing.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GWo\u001b[8Gktrunk m\u001b[17Gk\u001b[19Gs a new worktree for each branch and removes it on merge. Every bra\u001b[87Gch would start with \u001b[108Gmpty build\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Btree\u001b[10G:\u001b[12Gabout five\u001b[25Gld builds per gate, and Debug builds never\u001b[68Gshare objects\u001b[82Gbetween trees anyway.\u001b[104G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mPropos\u001b[10Gl:\u001b[13Gthre\u001b[19Gpermanent lanes, reused from task to task.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mLanes:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/jettison\u001b[39m (this checkout\u001b[76G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mne-b\u001b[81G\u001b[39mand\u001b[85G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/jettison.lane-c\u001b[39m,\u001b[113Gmade\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.015, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mI also w\u001b[12Gnt you to\u001b[22Gask the \u001b[31Gevi\u001b[35Gwer to be more thoroug\u001b[58G.\u001b[60GIt's\u001b[65Gtaking 3+ rounds\u001b[82Geach time to find unrelated errors.\u001b[118GI\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
