[0.053, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPropose a solution to the problem of waiting idle on the gate while each piece of work completes. I thought we set up\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mworktr\u001b[10Ges? Did y\u001b[20Gu\u001b[22Gonly set it up\u001b[37Gso\u001b[40Gone at a time could\u001b[60Gwork? Can you ex\u001b[77Gand it to have thr\u001b[96Ge worktrees in\u001b[111G\u001b[39m         \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mpa\u001b[6Gall\u001b[10Gl? One could be wai\u001b[30Ging\u001b[34Gon\u001b[37Gthe gate or\u001b[49Gadv\u001b[53Grsarial review, an\u001b[72Gth\u001b[75Gr could be having work\u001b[98Gactively performed on \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit, and a\u001b[13Gthird one\u001b[23Gif\u001b[26GI find I have sp\u001b[43Gr\u001b[46Gtime in between the first \u001b[73Gwo.\u001b[77GI want to make use of the caches that \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mcurre\u001b[9Gtly\u001b[13Gex\u001b[16Gst, so\u001b[23Greusing the\u001b[35Gs\u001b[37Gm\u001b[46Gworktrees from one run to\u001b[72Gan\u001b[75Gther would be good if it's not problematic.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, listed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m directory, ran \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mHere's\u001b[10Gthe\u001b[14Gworktree\u001b[23Gproposal.\u001b[33GI'll\u001b[38Gkeep\u001b[43Gworking\u001b[51Gon\u001b[54GJ01\u001b[58Gwhile\u001b[64Gyou\u001b[68Gread\u001b[73Git.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhy it's one at a time now.\u001b[31G\u001b[22mWorktrunk\u001b[41Gis\u001b[44Gset\u001b[48Gup,\u001b[52Gbut\u001b[56Gthere's\u001b[64Gonly\u001b[69Gone\u001b[73Gcheckout\u001b[82G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgit worktree list\u001b[101G\u001b[39mshows\u001b[107Gjust\u001b[112Gthis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bone). Two settings also work against reuse:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/.config/worktrunk/config.toml\u001b[39m puts new worktrees\u001b[56Gin\u001b[59G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/worktrees/jettison/<branch>\u001b[39m.\u001b[90Gccache\u001b[97Gonly\u001b[102Gshares\u001b[109Gcompiled\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gobjects between trees under \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects\u001b[39m (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCCACHE_BASEDIR\u001b[39m), so a worktree made there would s\u001b[95Gare nothing.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GWorktrunk mak\u001b[19Gs\u001b[21Ga n\u001b[25Gw\u001b[27Gworktree for each branch and remove\u001b[63G it\u001b[67Gon me\u001b[73Gg\u001b[75G. Ev\u001b[80Gry b\u001b[85Ganch would start w\u001b[104Gth empty\u001b[113Gbuild\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gtrees: about five\u001b[23Gcold builds per gate,\u001b[45Gand Debug builds never share objects between\u001b[90Gtrees\u001b[96Ganyway.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mProposal: three permanent lanes, reused from task to task.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m1. \u001b[1mLanes\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/jettison\u001b[39m (this checkout) plus \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/jettison.lane-b\u001b[81G\u001b[39mand\u001b[85G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/jettison.lane-c\u001b[39m,\u001b[113Gmade\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gonce with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgit worktree add\u001b[33G\u001b[39mand never remo\u001b[76G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mch -c <task> main\u001b[39m inside a free lane, so that\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
