[0.126, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m; every message after is XChaCha20-Poly1305 under a counter shared by both channels, the channel its a\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mdditional data, each channel taking only a counter above the last it opened, and the last counter used\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m once, then nothing more sealed. The secrets the engine keeps are wiped once spent. A hello that does \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnot open is refused as `KeyMismatch`. ENet's headers stay plain ([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mnetworking\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](../networking.md#the-wir\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me)). | Met: the `net` suite refuses a client pinning another server's key as `KeyMismatch` before its \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mcredential is judged, and admits the pinned one; it seals a credential that does not appear in the sea\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mled bytes, opens it once, and refuses it replayed, on the other channel, damaged, late on the unreliab\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mle channel, sealed by keys from another pinned key, and keys from a point of small order; it seals and\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m opens the last counter once and then refuses to seal; a raw ENet client is refused a hello recorded o\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mn another connection; two raw impostor servers, one offering the pinned public key as its fresh one an\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242md one proving a key of its own, are sent no hello and the client closes as `KeyMismatch`; every earlie\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mr case passes sealed. Each new case fails when its fix is undo\u001b[75G\u001b[49m\u001b[39m…\u001b[77G[+88\u001b[82Gchars]\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m                          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[2m 215 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 216 \u001b[22m Manifest's W18,\u001b[28GW11\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36GW19\u001b[40Gneeded\u001b[47Gno\u001b[50Gengine\u001b[57Gedit,\u001b[63Gand\u001b[67Glater\u001b[73GW12,\u001b[78GW13\u001b[82Gand\u001b[86GW14\u001b[90G(2026-11-23),\u001b[104Gcompetitiv\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m e\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 217 \u001b[22m procurement, regional governance and the close of its Stage 4, on the pin `14fc23a`. Its R01\r\u001b[10C\u001b[2B\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m \u001b[14Ghell command, recalling \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m memory, writing \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m memories…\r\u001b[75C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;233;154;122mBrewing…\u001b[13G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m27m 16s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m51.1k toke\u001b[36Gs)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle) · esc to inte\u001b[54Grupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
