\u001b[39G(`crypt\u001b[47G_kx`\u001b[52Gtwic\u001b[57G,\u001b[62Ged BLAKE2b), the server's offer ca\u001b[97Gries\u001b[102Ga proof seal\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bed with the connection's keys, and the hello,\u001b[58Gits credenti\u001b[71Gl\u001b[73Gwith\u001b[78Git, goes sealed only once\u001b[104Gthe proof \r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bope\u001b[16Gs, so\u001b[22Ga replayed hello does n\u001b[46Gt \u001b[49Gpen and no\u001b[60Gcr\u001b[63Gdential \u001b[72Goes to a server that doe\u001b[98Gnot\u001b[102Ghold the key\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B;\u001b[14Gev\u001b[17Gry message\u001b[28Gafter is XChaCha20-Poly1305\u001b[56Gunder\u001b[63G counter shared by both\u001b[87Gchannels, t\u001b[99Ge channel its a\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bdditional data, each ch\u001b[36Gnnel taking\u001b[48Gonly a counter\u001b[63Gabove the last it opened,\u001b[89Gand\u001b[93Gthe\u001b[97Glast\u001b[102Gcounter\u001b[110Gused\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m once, then nothing more sealed. The secrets the engine keeps are wiped once spent. A hello that does \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnot open is refused as `KeyMismatch`. ENet's headers stay plain ([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mnetworking\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](../networking.md#the-wir\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me)). | Met: the `net` suite refuses a client pinning another server's key as `KeyMismatch` before its \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mcredential is judged, and admits the pinned one; it seals a credential that does not appear in the sea\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mled bytes, opens it once, and refus\u001b[76Gchannel, damaged, late on the unreliab\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
