[0.070, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mI prefer for all the work to be based on the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m branch rather than main. When work is merged successfully \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mand tested on \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m then it is a candiate for merging into main. Everything else is approved. Build it when \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255myou're ready.\u001b[39m                                                                                                         \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mGot\u001b[7Git:\u001b[11Glanes\u001b[17Gbranch\u001b[24Gfrom\u001b[29G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[39m,\u001b[43Gwork\u001b[48Gmerges\u001b[55Gback\u001b[60Ginto\u001b[65G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[39m,\u001b[79Gand\u001b[83Gonly\u001b[88Gwork\u001b[93Gtested\u001b[100Gthere\u001b[106Gis\u001b[109Ga\u001b[111Gcandidate\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gfor \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mmain\u001b[39m. I'll set up the lanes once J01 is\u001b[47Gcommit\u001b[54Ged.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/networking.md)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m7\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 108 \u001b[22m client seals; the second means a server's secret taken later opens no recorded connection, since\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 109 \u001b[22m both fresh secrets are wiped once the keys are made.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 110 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 111 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mThe client then sends its hello, sealed. It is a binary archive, format `jettison.hello` version 1,   \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 111 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mThe server's offer carries a *proof*: a message with no body sealed with the connection's keys,       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 112 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwhich only the holder of the pinned secret can make. The client checks it before it sends anything    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 113 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mmore, and closes as `KeyMismatch` i\u001b[76Gt, a server that did not hold the     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
