[0.049, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G  build through it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mReview base:\u001b[18G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcross-review.sh\u001b[34G\u001b[39mnow\u001b[38Gcompares\u001b[47Gagainst\u001b[55G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[68G\u001b[39mby\u001b[71Gdefault.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mWorktrunk path:\u001b[22m I changed it in your dotfiles (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/.dotfil\u001b[62Gs/.config/worktrunk/config.toml\u001b[39m) to\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m~/projects/<repo>.<branch>\u001b[39m, so any worktree it makes shares cc\u001b[68Gche.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mWarm builds:\u001b[18G\u001b[22mengine\u001b[25Glanes\u001b[31GB\u001b[33Gand\u001b[37GC\u001b[39Geach\u001b[44Gran\u001b[48Ga\u001b[50Gfull\u001b[55Gcold\u001b[60Ggate\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gboth\u001b[74Gpassed,\u001b[82Gin\u001b[85Gabout\u001b[91G18\u001b[94Gminutes\u001b[102Geach,\u001b[108Gso\u001b[111Gtheir\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bbuild\u001b[11Gtrees\u001b[17Gare\u001b[21Gwarm.\u001b[27GManifest's\u001b[38Glanes\u001b[44Gare\u001b[48Gparked\u001b[55Gon\u001b[58G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[71G\u001b[39mbut\u001b[75Gnot\u001b[79Gbuilt,\u001b[86Gso\u001b[89Gtheir\u001b[95Gfirst\u001b[101Gbuild\u001b[107Gwill\u001b[112Gbe\u001b[115Gcold.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G  Manifest's lane change was only syntax-checked,\u001b[53Gnot\u001b[57Grun\u001b[61Gthrough\u001b[69Gits\u001b[73Ggate.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mLane state:\u001b[17G\u001b[22meach\u001b[22Glane\u001b[27Ghas\u001b[31Ga\u001b[33G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/lane.md\u001b[47G\u001b[39msaying\u001b[54Gwhat\u001b[59Git\u001b[62Gholds.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mOne risk:\u001b[22m a process left running by a killed gate, such as a stray Xvfb, keeps the lock until it exits. \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mheavy.sh\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  prints that it's waiting, so a stuck queue shows up.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mNext:\u001b[22m Manifest's adoption of J01 (the server key file, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--key\u001b[39m, and the public key in the test builds' client config),\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  in lane A. I'd use Opus at high effort, because it's trust-boundary and file-permission work. Now is a good point to\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m/compact\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSautéed for 1h 22m 14s · done 10:26 am\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mLet's revise the way the worktrees will be used. I see there are\u001b[68Gsix total now, including the ones that are provided \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mby the primary source code folder i.e. ~/projects/jettison and ~/projects/manifest . I want the primary one to be \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mused for merging in work from the two secondary worktrees for each project. You will continue to orchestrate from the\u001b[39m \u001b[49m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m❯ I prefer for all the work to be based on the `feature-base` branch rather than main. When work is merged successfull…\u001b[39m \r\u001b[46C\u001b[20B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m Jump to bottom (ctrl+End) ↓ \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
