[0.812, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWarm builds:\u001b[22m engine lanes B\u001b[33Gand C each ran a full cold gate\u001b[65Gand both\u001b[74Gpassed,\u001b[82Gin\u001b[85Gabout\u001b[91G18\u001b[94Gminutes\u001b[102Geach,\u001b[108Gso\u001b[111Gtheir\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gbuild trees are warm. Manifest's lanes\u001b[44Gare\u001b[48Gparked\u001b[55Gon \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[39m but not built, s\u001b[88G \u001b[90Gheir first build will b\u001b[114G cold.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BManifest's l\u001b[18Gn\u001b[21Gchange was only syntax-ch\u001b[47Gcked, not run through its gate.\u001b[79G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mLane state:\u001b[22m each l\u001b[25Ge has a \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/lane.md\u001b[39m saying what it \u001b[63Golds.\u001b[69G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mOne risk:\u001b[13G\u001b[22ma\u001b[15Gprocess\u001b[23Gleft\u001b[28Grunning\u001b[36Gby\u001b[39Ga\u001b[41Gkilled\u001b[48Ggate,\u001b[54Gsuch\u001b[59Gas\u001b[62Ga\u001b[64Gstray\u001b[70GXvfb,\u001b[76Gkeeps\u001b[82Gthe\u001b[86Glock\u001b[91Guntil\u001b[97Git\u001b[100Gexits.\u001b[107G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mheavy.sh\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39mprints that\u001b[15Git's waiting, so a stuck queue shows up.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mNext:\u001b[9G\u001b[22mManifest's\u001b[20Gadoption\u001b[29Gof\u001b[32GJ01\u001b[36G(the\u001b[41Gserver\u001b[48Gkey\u001b[52Gfile,\u001b[58G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--key\u001b[39m,\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gthe\u001b[73Gpublic\u001b[80Gkey\u001b[84Gin\u001b[87Gthe\u001b[91Gtest\u001b[96Gbuilds'\u001b[104Gclient\u001b[111Gconfig),\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bin lane A. I'd use O\u001b[24Gus at high effort, becaus\u001b[50G it's trust-boundary and file-p\u001b[82Grm\u001b[85Gssion\u001b[91Gwork. Now is\u001b[104Ga good\u001b[111Gp\u001b[113Gint to\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m/compact\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GSautéed for 1h 22m 14s · done 10:26 am\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mLet's revise the way the worktrees will be used. I see there are six total now, including the ones that are provided \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mby the pr\u001b[13Gmary source code fold\u001b[35Gr i.e. ~/proj\u001b[49Gcts/jettison and ~/projec\u001b[75Gs/manifest . I wan\u001b[94G the primary\u001b[107Gon\u001b[111Gto be \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mused for merging in work from the\u001b[37Gtwo secondary work\u001b[56Grees for each project. You will\u001b[88Gcontinue to orchestrate from\u001b[117Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bprimary folders.\u001b[20GKeep the mechanisms you proposed for d\u001b[59Gtermining which worktree to use when a new task is sta\u001b[114Gted. \u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mAnd gate the \u001b[17Geally heavy\u001b[29Gtasks like\u001b[40Gthe\u001b[44Gfull gate and clang builds as you do now.\u001b[39m                                  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                            \u001b[76G         \u001b[49m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
